          "path": "_m/u/1/4/0/mines-in-the-battle-of-messines-1917-wp/disturbing-image-destr.jpg",
          "filename": "NLS Haig - Smashed up German trench on Messines Ridge with dead.jpg",
          "caption": "This is a disturbing image of a destroyed German trench. In the foreground the limp bodies of dead German soldiers lie amidst the rubble. It is difficult to distinguish the soldiers from the chaos around them, but four bodies are clearly visible. One man, wearing a helmet, has been pushed forward by the blast and, although dead, appears to crouch forward. The entire scene is a maelstrom of mud, splintered wood and dead bodies.Original reads: 'OFFICIAL PHOTOGRAPHS TAKEN ON THE BRITISH WESTERN FRONT. Smashed up German trench on Messines Ridge with dead.'Photographs from the Haig \"Official Photographs\" series",
